      <uighur>abisik</uighur>
      <cyrillic>авшиг</cyrillic>
      <transcript>ABISIG</transcript>
      <definition>[= abisiγ, S. abhiçeka] n. Consecration by . sprinkling holy water, consecration in general (as of kings, buddhas, saintly persons, laymen); powers conferred through consecration or blessings; ordainment.</definition>
      <page>4</page>
      <examples>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠠᠪᠢᠰᠢᠭ ᠠᠪᠬᠤ</unicode>
          <transcript>-- abxu</transcript>
          <definition>To receive consecration or ordainment.</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠠᠪᠢᠰᠢᠭ ᠣᠯᠬᠤ</unicode>
          <transcript>-- olxu</transcript>
          <definition>To receive consecration or ordainment.</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠠᠪᠢᠰᠢᠭ ᠥᠭᠺᠦ</unicode>
          <transcript>-- øgky</transcript>
          <definition>To bestow .consecration, ordain a monk or priest.</definition>
        </example>
      </examples>
    </entry_item>
